# Claude instances - EXAMPLE
#
# Copy to instances.conf and edit:
#
#     cp instances.conf.example instances.conf
#
# instances.conf is gitignored, since slugs and organisation names are specific
# to your machine. Keep this example generic when you change its format.
#
# One row per additional organisation. The default /Applications/Claude.app and
# ~/.claude are NOT listed here - they are the personal profile and are never
# touched by this tooling.
#
# Columns (whitespace separated):
#
#   slug    lowercase id. Drives ~/.claude-<slug>, the `claude-<slug>` command
#           and the bundle id com.anthropic.claude.<slug>.
#   label   short name. Drives "Claude <label>.app", the Electron helper names
#           and the letters drawn on the icon. Keep it to 2-4 characters so it
#           stays legible at 32px.
#   hue     icon tint. 100 leaves Claude's orange unchanged; each step rotates
#           the hue by 1.8 degrees, so 200 is the opposite side of the wheel.
#           Handy values: 65 purple, 72 pink, 150 green, 200 blue, 250 magenta.
#           Keep instances ~60 apart so they read differently.
#   note    free text, ignored by the scripts.
#
# After editing run:  claude-sync
# then `claude-rebuild <slug>` for any instance whose app does not exist yet.
#
# The slug `personal` is reserved: that instance uses the stock profile
# (~/.claude and ~/Library/Application Support/Claude), so it opens the same
# account Claude.app itself does, and it is always built as a launcher. Give it
# a row and launch it from its own icon rather than from Claude.app, which
# collides with launcher instances.
#
# slug  label  hue  note
acme    ACME   72   Acme Corp
beta    BTA    200  Beta Industries
personal ME     100  stock ~/.claude profile (hue 100 = Claude orange, untinted)
